{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_19-38-40-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && grep -n -i \\\"snapshot\\\\|transfer\\\\|lease\\\\|non-voter\\\\|nonvoter\\\\|prevote\\\\|pre-vote\\\\|deadlock\\\\|stuck\\\\|hang\\\\|voter\\\" CHANGELOG.md | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"1:# UNRELEASED\n9:CHANGES\n15:* Raft pre-vote extension implementation, activated by default. [GH-530](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/530)\n23:CHANGES\n34:* Fix rare leadership transfer failures when writes happen during transfer. [GH-581](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/581)\n38:CHANGES\n56:* Race with `candidateFromLeadershipTransfer` [GH-570](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/570)\n62:* Fixed a performance anomaly related to pipelining RPCs that caused large increases in commit latency under high write throughput. Default behavior has changed. For more information see #541.\n67:* Support log stores with a monotonically increasing index.  Implementing a log store with the `MonotonicLogStore` interface where `IsMonotonic()` returns true will allow Raft to clear all previous logs on user restores of Raft snapshots.\n70:* Restoring a snapshot with the raft-wal log store caused a panic due to index gap that is created during snapshot restores.\n77:* Made `TrailingLogs`, `SnapshotInterval` and `SnapshotThreshold` reloadable at runtime using a new `ReloadConfig` method. This allows recovery from cases where there are not enough logs retained for followers to catchup after a restart. [[GH-444](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/444)]\n91:* Allow futures to react to `Shutdown()` to prevent a deadlock with `takeSnapshot()` [[GH-390](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/390)]\n92:* Prevent non-voters from becoming eligible for leadership elections [[GH-398](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/398)]\n93:* Remove an unneeded `io.Copy` from snapshot writes [[GH-399](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/399)]\n96:* Reject leadership transfer requests when in candidate state to prevent indefinite blocking while unable to elect a leader [[GH-413](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/413)]\n121:* Fix snapshot to not attempt to truncate a negative range [[GH-358](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/358)]\n129:* Add config option to skip snapshot restore on startup [[GH-340](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/340)]\n145:* Add transfer leadership extension [[GH-306](https://github.com/hashicorp/raft/pull/306)]\n151:* Add peer changes to observations [[GH-326](https://github.com/hashicorp/consul/pull/326)]\n155:* Copy the contents of an InmemSnapshotStore when opening a snapshot [[GH-270](https://github.com/hashicorp/consul/pull/270)]\n169:v1.0.0 takes the changes that were staged in the library-v2-stage-one branch. This version manages server identities using a UUID, so introduces some breaking API changes. It also versions the Raft protocol, and requires some special steps when interoperating with Raft servers running older versions of the library (see the detailed comment in config.go about version compatibility). You can reference https://github.com/hashicorp/consul/pull/2222 for an idea of what was required to port Consul to these new interfaces.\n173:v0.1.0 is the original stable version of the library that was in main and has been maintained with no breaking API changes. This was in use by Consul prior to version 0.7.0.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
